# C++ / Hydra Patterns

## HdxTask lifecycle

Custom render tasks extend `pxr::HdxTask`:

```cpp
void _Sync(HdSceneDelegate* delegate, HdTaskContext* ctx, HdDirtyBits* dirtyBits) override;
void Prepare(HdTaskContext* ctx, HdRenderIndex* renderIndex) override;
void Execute(HdTaskContext* ctx) override;
```

- `_Sync`: read params from scene delegate when `DirtyParams`; clear dirty bits
- `Prepare`: preprocessing before execution
- `Execute`: run shaders / composite passes

## Params structs

- One params struct per task (e.g. `BlurTaskParams`)
- Provide `operator==` — used for dirty tracking in tests and task manager
- Register via `TaskManager::AddTask<T>(token, commitFn, ...)`
- Commit functions update params each frame (size, camera, app state)

## Task wiring

- Pass data between tasks through `HdTaskContext` string tokens (texture names), not direct pointers
- Insert tasks relative to existing ones: `TaskManager::InsertionOrder::insertBefore` / `insertAfter`
- Shaders live in `include/hvt/resources/shaders/` as `.glslfx` files

## Style

- Match surrounding code style and naming
- Use `HVT_API` on exported free functions, not on classes
- Prefer extending existing tasks/helpers over duplicating Hydra boilerplate
- Keep changes minimal — one concern per PR
